.TH QUICKSILVER-TX "1" "September 2026" "quicksilver-tx v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quicksilver-tx \- manual page for quicksilver-tx v0.1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quicksilver-tx
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,<hex-tx> \/\fR[\fI\,commands\/\fR]
.br
.B quicksilver-tx
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,-create \/\fR[\fI\,commands\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
quicksilver\-tx version v0.1.0
.PP
The quicksilver\-tx tool is used for creating and modifying Quicksilver transactions.
.PP
quicksilver\-tx can be used with "<hex\-tx> [commands]" to update a hex\-encoded Quicksilver transaction, or with "\-create [commands]" to create a hex\-encoded Quicksilver transaction.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-create\fR
.IP
Create new, empty TX.
.HP
\fB\-help\fR
.IP
Print this help message and exit (also \fB\-h\fR or \-?)
.HP
\fB\-json\fR
.IP
Select JSON output
.HP
\fB\-txid\fR
.IP
Output only the hex\-encoded transaction id of the resultant transaction.
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.PP
Debugging/Testing options:
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-chain=\fR<chain>
.IP
Use the chain <chain> (default: main). Allowed values: main, publictest,
sandbox
.HP
\fB\-publictest\fR
.IP
Use the Quicksilver Public Test Network. Equivalent to
\fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,publictest\/\fR.
.PP
Commands:
.IP
delin=N
.IP
Delete input N from TX
.IP
delout=N
.IP
Delete output N from TX
.IP
in=TXID:VOUT(:SEQUENCE_NUMBER)
.IP
Add input to TX
.IP
locktime=N
.IP
Set TX lock time to N
.IP
nversion=N
.IP
Set TX version to N
.IP
outaddr=VALUE:ADDRESS
.IP
Add address\-based output to TX
.IP
outdata=[VALUE:]DATA
.IP
Add data\-based output to TX
.IP
outmultisig=VALUE:REQUIRED:PUBKEYS:PUBKEY1:PUBKEY2:....[:FLAGS]
.IP
Add Pay To n\-of\-m Multi\-sig output to TX. n = REQUIRED, m = PUBKEYS.
Optionally add the "W" flag to produce a P2WSH output. Optionally
add the "S" flag to wrap a non\-witness output in P2SH. The flags
are mutually exclusive.
.IP
outpubkey=VALUE:PUBKEY[:FLAGS]
.IP
Add pay\-to\-pubkey output to TX. Optionally add the "W" flag to produce a
P2WPKH output. Optionally add the "S" flag to wrap a non\-witness
output in P2SH. The flags are mutually exclusive.
.IP
outscript=VALUE:SCRIPT[:FLAGS]
.IP
Add raw script output to TX. Optionally add the "W" flag to produce a
P2WSH output. Optionally add the "S" flag to wrap a non\-witness
output in P2SH. The flags are mutually exclusive.
.IP
sign=SIGHASH\-FLAGS
.IP
Add zero or more signatures to transaction. This command requires JSON
registers:prevtxs=JSON object, privatekeys=JSON object. See
signrawtransactionwithkey docs for format of sighash flags, JSON
objects.
.PP
Register Commands:
.IP
load=NAME:FILENAME
.IP
Load JSON file FILENAME into register NAME
.IP
set=NAME:JSON\-STRING
.IP
Set register NAME to given JSON\-STRING
